We now prove the claim that $\bar z <\infty$ almost surely. Let $z_0\in\mathbb{R}$ be such that $\mathfrak{h}_0(z_0) > -\infty$. It is enough to prove that $\mathfrak{h}_0(z_0) + \inf_{s\in[T_0,T]}\inf_{|y|\leq K} \mathcal L(z_0,0;y,s) =: -R > -\infty$, i.e., $R<\infty$, and that there exists a random constant $M$ depending on only $T_0$, $T$, and $K$ such that $\sup_{|z| \geq M} (\mathfrak{h}_0(z)+\mathcal L(z,0;y,s)) < -R$ for all $|y|\leq K$.

