&\leq \alpha-\gamma |z|^{1/2} + F_{1/3}(z,0,K,T) - \frac{(z-y)^2}{T_0}.
\end{align*}

It is easy to see that we can find $M$ large enough depending on only $\alpha$, $\gamma$, $K$, $T$ and $T_0$ such that $|z| > M$ implies that the previous expression is smaller than $-R$  for all $y$ with $|y|\leq K$. This completes the proof of the claim, and thus of  Lemma~\ref{lem:Holder-space}.

